<%# Which of its agents' calls ask a person first (Workspace::ApprovalPolicy): its owner chooses, or leaves it to the
    install; everyone in it reads which. What asks everywhere, and each agent's Always, are on the agent's Permissions. -%>
<%# locals: (workspace:) -%>
<% policy = workspace.approvals %>
<section class="ui-group" aria-labelledby="approval_policy_title" id="approval_policy">
  <h2 class="ui-group__title" id="approval_policy_title">Approvals</h2>
  <ul class="ui-group__rows">
    <% if workspace.owner == Current.user %>
      <li class="ui-row">
        <%= form_with model: workspace, url: workspace_approval_policy_path(workspace), method: :patch, scope: :workspace, class: "ui-row__form" do |form| %>
          <%= form.label :approval_policy, class: "ui-row__label" do %>
            Its agents<span class="ui-row__detail">What they ask you before doing.</span>
          <% end %>
          <span class="ui-row__value">
            <%= form.select :approval_policy,
                  [ [ "Install's default: #{Workspace::ApprovalPolicy.new(Workspace::ApprovalPolicy.install_default).to_s.downcase_first}", "" ],
                    *Workspace::ApprovalPolicy::CHOICES.invert ],
                  { selected: workspace.approval_policy.to_s }, class: "ui-row__select" %>
            <%= form.submit "Save", class: "button", data: { variant: "ghost", size: "sm" } %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% else %>
      <li class="ui-row">
        <p class="ui-row__label">
          <%= policy %><%= " (the install's default)" unless workspace.approval_policy %>
          <span class="ui-row__detail">Its owner chooses what its agents ask before doing.</span>
        </p>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <% workspace.errors.full_messages_for(:approval_policy).each do |message| %>
    <p class="field__error"><%= message %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p class="ui-group__help">
    <% if policy.everything? %>
      Its agents do what they are asked without a card, even what reaches other people.
    <% elsif policy.allow? %>
      Its agents do what they are asked without a card, except what asks every time, such as an iMessage from your phone.
    <% elsif policy.others? %>
      Its agents ask first before what reaches other people (an email, a text, a Campfire or Concourse message, an
      invitation to an event, a sign-in with a saved password) and before removing a routine.
      Changes to their own instructions follow the separate setting.
    <% else %>
      Its agents ask first before anything that changes something outside them, unless you answered "Always".
    <% end %>
    Payments and sign-ins still show a card under every policy, as does the first call with each saved API key. Each agent's Permissions lists what else it asks.
    Each call is recorded in its thread.
  </p>
</section>
